# =============================================================================
# ai-gateway.env — real API keys for the credential gateway
# =============================================================================
# 1. Copy this file to:   ~/.ai-secrets/ai-gateway.env   (on the Mac)
# 2. Fill in the providers you use (leave the rest commented out).
# 3. Lock it down:        chmod 600 ~/.ai-secrets/ai-gateway.env
# 4. Apply:              just seed-secrets
#
# These keys are injected by the gateway (gateway/Caddyfile) into outbound
# requests from sandboxes. For gateway-routed providers, sandboxes hold only
# dummy keys (sandbox/compose.sandbox.yaml + baked CLI configs). Direct BYOK
# is the explicit exception.
# Keep this file OUT of any synced/git location — it lives outside the
# repo AND outside ~/ai-projects on purpose; the VM only ever sees it
# read-only (/mnt/secrets).
# =============================================================================

# --- primary providers ---------------------------------------------------------

# OpenCode Go subscription API key (routes /opencode-go — OpenCode flavor)
REAL_OPENCODE_API_KEY=

# DeepSeek official API key (routes /deepseek — deepseek flavor, ad-hoc tools)
REAL_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# --- gateway-isolated third-party provider template (disabled) ------------------
# To isolate another provider's key:
#   1. Uncomment/rename below and add the matching route block in
#      gateway/Caddyfile (the commented /foo template).
#   2. In OpenCode, point that provider's baseURL at
#      http://host.docker.internal:4000/foo/v1 with a dummy apiKey.
#   3. Run: just seed-secrets && just gateway-reload
# See docs/AGENT-CONFIG.md → "Gateway-isolated third-party provider".
# REAL_FOO_API_KEY=
